# hi-ai Troubleshooting Guide

If you're running the hi-ai installer and things don't go as planned, here's a quick reference to fix common issues.

---

## 🔑 Step 1: Get Your OpenAI API Key
hi-ai needs your OpenAI API key to function.

1. Go to: [https://platform.openai.com/account/api-keys](https://platform.openai.com/account/api-keys)
2. Log in and click **"Create new secret key"**
3. Copy it and save it somewhere safe
4. When hi-ai first runs, it will ask for this key

---

## 🛠️ If The Installer Fails...

### 1. ❌ Pip refuses to install packages
Zorin OS has pip restrictions. You need to install these:

```bash
sudo apt install python3-venv python3-full -y
```

Then rerun the installer.

---

### 2. ❌ "No module named openai"
If hi-ai runs but fails on the first command:

```bash
source ~/.hi-ai-env/bin/activate
pip install --break-system-packages openai==0.28
```

---

### 3. ❌ `hi-ai: command not found`
The launcher may be missing. Create it manually:

```bash
sudo ln -s /home/$USER/.hi-ai.py /usr/local/bin/hi-ai
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/hi-ai
```

If that doesn't work:
```bash
sudo nano /usr/local/bin/hi-ai
```
Paste this:
```bash
#!/bin/bash
source /home/$USER/.hi-ai-env/bin/activate
python3 /home/$USER/.hi-ai.py
```
Then:
```bash
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/hi-ai
```

---

## ✅ After These Fixes
Type:
```bash
hi-ai
```
You should see:
```
🧠 Nexus is online. Type anything. Type 'exit' to quit.
```

You're now good to go. Welcome to the hi-ai system.

